hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22882","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Jarir, meaning Ibn Hazim, narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Dawud ibn Husayn, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Abi Uqbah, from Abu Uqbah, and he was a freedman of the people of Persia, who said: I witnessed with the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the day of Uhud. So I struck a man of the polytheists and said: Take it from me, and I am the Persian boy. So it reached the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he said: Why did you not say: Take it from me, and I am the Ansari boy."
